## Why This Is Asked
Tests a clean DP formulation for segmentation with per-placement costs and wildcards. It also probes backtracking and memoization versus tabulation choices under a dictionary constraint.

## Key Concepts
- DP on string positions with a dictionary
- Memoization vs bottom-up tabulation
- Backtracking reconstruction of segmentation
- Handling wildcards and per-placement costs

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCost(s, dict) {
  const n = s.length;
  const memo = new Array(n+1).fill(null);
  const choice = new Array(n).fill(null);

  function costAt(i, w) {
    let cost = 0;
    for (let j = 0; j < w.length; j++) {
      if (s[i+j] !== '?' && s[i+j] !== w[j]) {
        cost++;
      }
    }
    return cost;
  }

  function dp(i) {
    if (i === n) return 0;
    if (memo[i] !== null) return memo[i];

    let best = Infinity;
    let bestWord = null;

    for (const w of dict) {
      if (i + w.length <= n) {
        const c = costAt(i, w) + dp(i + w.length);
        if (c < best) {
          best = c;
          bestWord = w;
        }
      }
    }

    memo[i] = best;
    choice[i] = bestWord;
    return best;
  }

  const minCost = dp(0);
  if (minCost === Infinity) return -1;

  // Reconstruct segmentation
  const words = [];
  let i = 0;
  while (i < n) {
    words.push(choice[i]);
    i += choice[i].length;
  }

  return { cost: minCost, words };
}
```

## Complexity
Time: O(n × sum|w|) where sum|w| is total length of all dictionary words
Space: O(n) for memoization and choice arrays

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to derive a recurrence for a simple constraint (no adjacent picks), then implement both top-down memoization and bottom-up tabulation. Requires correct base cases for N=0 and N=1 and translating to iterative state transitions. Follow-up prompts space optimization and practical coding habits.

## Key Concepts
- DP for non-adjacent max sum (House Robber)
- Top-down memoization with base cases
- Bottom-up tabulation
- Space optimization to O(1)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxNonAdjacent(nums){
  const n = nums.length;
  if (n === 0) return 0;
  const memo = Array(n).fill(-1);
  const solve = i => {
    if (i < 0) return 0;
    if (memo[i] !== -1) return memo[i];
    memo[i] = Math.max(nums[i] + solve(i-2), solve(i-1));
    return memo[i];
  };
  return solve(n-1);
}
function maxNonAdjacentTab(nums){
  const n = nums.length;
  if (n === 0) return 0;
  let prev2 = 0, prev1 = Math.max(0, nums[0]);
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++){
    const cur = Math.max(prev1, nums[i] + prev2);
    prev2 = prev1;
    prev1 = cur;
  }
  return prev1;
}
```

