Why This Is Asked\n\nThis question probes understanding of practical sorting trade-offs beyond textbook asymptotics, including cache locality, in-place constraints, and robust pivot strategies. It invites discussion of 3-way partitioning to handle duplicates, median-of-three to curb worst-case behavior, and a small insertion sort for tiny partitions.\n\n## Key Concepts\n- 3-way partitioning in quicksort\n- median-of-three pivot selection\n- insertion sort threshold tuning\n- in-place algorithms and cache efficiency\n- iterative vs recursive implementations\n\n## Code Example\n```javascript
function sortInPlace(arr){
  const TH = 16;
  const swap=(a,i,j)=>{const t=a[i]; a[i]=a[j]; a[j]=t;};
  const medianOfThree=(a,i,j,k)=>{let x=[a[i],i],[a[j],j],[a[k],k].sort((p,q)=>p[0]-q[0]); return a[x[1]];};
  // iterative 3-way quicksort skeleton
  const stack=[[0,arr.length-1]];
  while(stack.length){
    const [lo,hi]=stack.pop();
    if(hi-lo+1<=TH){ // insertion sort for small partitions
      for(let i=lo+1;i<=hi;i++){
        let t=arr[i], j=i-1;
        while(j>=lo && arr[j]>t){ arr[j+1]=arr[j]; j-- }
        arr[j+1]=t;
      }
      continue;
    }
    // median-of-three pivot
    const mid=(lo+hi)>>1;
    const pivot= medianOfThree(arr, lo, mid, hi);
    // 3-way partition
    let lt=lo, i=lo, gt=hi;
    while(i<=gt){
      if(arr[i]<pivot) swap(arr, lt++, i++);
      else if(arr[i]>pivot) swap(arr, i, gt--);
      else i++;
    }
    stack.push([lo, lt-1]);
    stack.push([gt+1, hi]);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Models real build/dependency graphs where costs accumulate; asks for both memoized and tabular DP to compare patterns and understand trade-offs. Emphasizes modulo arithmetic and edge-case handling for unreachable sinks and tight budgets.

## Key Concepts

- DP on DAG with an extra weight dimension
- Top-down memoization with (node, remainingBudget)
- Bottom-up DP in topological order with weight axis
- Modulo arithmetic and edge-case handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Top-down memoized DFS
function countPaths(n, edges, W) {
  const adj = Array.from({length: n}, () => []);
  for (const [u, v, w] of edges) adj[u].push([v, w]);
  const memo = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(W + 1).fill(-1));
  const dfs = (u, rem) => {
    if (u === n - 1) return 1;
    if (memo[u][rem] !== -1) return memo[u][rem];
    let res = 0;
    for (const [v, w] of adj[u]) if (w <= rem) res = (res + dfs(v, rem - w)) % 1_000_000_007;
    return memo[u][rem] = res;
  };
  return dfs(0, W);
}
```

```javascript
// Bottom-up DP in topological order
function countPathsBottomUp(n, edges, W) {
  const adj = Array.from({length: n}, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0);
  for (const [u, v, w] of edges) {
    adj[u].push([v, w]);
    indeg[v]++;
  }
  // Kahn's algorithm for topo order
  const q = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  const topo = [];
  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift(); topo.push(u);
    for (const [v] of adj[u]) if (--indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(W + 1).fill(0));
  dp[0][0] = 1;
  for (const u of topo) {
    for (const [v, w] of adj[u]) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= W - w; t++) {
        if (dp[u][t] !== 0) dp[v][t + w] = (dp[v][t + w] + dp[u][t]) % 1_000_000_007;
      }
    }
  }
  let ans = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t <= W; t++) ans = (ans + dp[n - 1][t]) % 1_000_000_007;
  return ans;
}
```

